# Normalize line endings to LF on checkout for every text file. The codebase
# is developed on macOS/Linux and assumes LF (e.g. theme-contract.test.tsx
# regexes over app.css with embedded "\n"). Without this, Git for Windows'
# default core.autocrlf=true rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout, which
# breaks content-comparison tests. The binary overrides below take precedence
# for the listed globs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary asset handling.
#
# Tag image / icon / packaging artifacts as binary so git doesn't
# try to text-diff them on every regeneration (README screenshot
# captures, vendor brand-kit refreshes, packaging builds) and
# doesn't apply EOL conversion on Windows checkouts.

**/*.png binary
**/*.gif binary
**/*.jpg binary
**/*.jpeg binary
**/*.ico binary
**/*.icns binary
**/*.webp binary

# Vendor brand-kit SVGs — verbatim files from each vendor's brand
# kit, refreshed via the procedure documented in each vendor's
# `README.md` and never hand-edited (see
# `apps/desktop/CLAUDE.md` → "Third-Party Brand Assets" for the rule).
# Treat as binary so vendor refreshes don't show noisy XML diffs.
apps/desktop/src/renderer/src/assets/**/*.svg binary
